# Project Goal: Inventory Management System for Food & Beverage Operations

## Vision
Build a **web-based Inventory Management System** that gives end-to-end visibility and control of inventory—from **procurement and supplier management** to **production consumption**, **stock movements**, and **financial tracking**—so the business can **optimize stock**, **minimize waste**, and **improve operational efficiency**.

---

## Primary Objectives
- Maintain **accurate, real-time stock levels** across all inventory items (ingredients, finished goods, packaging).
- Reduce **waste/spoilage** and prevent **over-ordering** with thresholds, capacity rules, and forecasting.
- Streamline purchasing with **PO workflows** and **intelligent supplier selection**.
- Ensure traceability via a complete **audit log** of inventory transactions.
- Provide decision support through **reports, alerts, and cost metrics** (COGS, valuation).

---

## MVP Scope (Must-Have)
### 1) Core Inventory Management
- **Item Master**
  - Central catalog for finished products, ingredients, and packaging.
  - Unique SKU/item code.
  - Support a **product matrix / BOM-style relationships** (ingredients → finished goods).
- **Packaging Components**
  - Store packaging specifications (dimensions, material, label/sticker details).
- **Stock Control**
  - Real-time stock by item.
  - Per-item configurable rules:
    - Total storage capacity
    - Minimum threshold (% of capacity)
    - Purchase allowance (% of capacity) to prevent over-ordering
- **Inventory Movements**
  - Track movement types:
    - Production consumption
    - Returns (supplier/customer)
    - Transfers (future multi-location readiness)
    - Calculated losses (waste, spoilage, pilferage, damages)
- **Accountability Log (Audit Trail)**
  - Log every movement with timestamp + user responsible.

### 2) Procurement & Supplier Management
- **Supplier Database**
  - Maintain suppliers and allow **alternative suppliers per ingredient/material**.
- **Intelligent Supplier Selection**
  - Recommend supplier based on prioritized criteria:
    1. Price
    2. MOQ compatibility
    3. Ability to consolidate the most required items into one order
- **Supplier Performance Tracking**
  - Track/edit metrics tied to deliveries/batches:
    - Delivery time
    - Quality control ratings
    - Price consistency
  - Flag suppliers below a defined performance threshold.
- **Purchase Order (PO) Management**
  - Create POs and record receiving with item-level breakdown.
  - Handle supplier-specific MOQs and bulk discounts.

### 3) Production & Operations
- **Job Order (JO) Management**
  - Create/track JOs for production.
  - On JO completion:
    - Automatically **deduct consumed ingredients**
    - Automatically **add finished goods to stock**
  - Record detailed JO breakdown.

### 4) Forecasting, Notifications & Analytics
- **Automated Forecasting**
  - Forecast ingredient availability; highlight surplus/shortage to keep “just right” inventory.
- **Alerts & Notifications**
  - Low stock threshold reached
  - Monthly procurement reminders (1 week before month start)
  - Supplier quality/performance flags
- **Reporting Suite**
  - Stock aging (slow-moving/expiring risk)
  - Surplus & shortage reports
  - Full history of inventory movements

### 5) Financial Tracking
- **Cost Analysis**
  - Cost per unit (items)
  - Total inventory valuation
